	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Keyword: rx [query]

Lists every tab of every Rex session, on this Mac and on each host in `rex hosts`.
Matches session, tab name, terminal title, directory and host; all words must match.

↵  jump to the tab in Rex
⇧ / ⌘Y  Quick Look preview of the tab's screen
⌘↵  close the tab (asks first)
⌥↵  copy the session and tab IDs
Last row: ↵ creates a local session named after the query.

Remote hosts take a few seconds to snapshot, so results come from a cache that
refreshes in the background whenever it's older than refresh_seconds.

Variables:
  rex_path         path to the rex CLI (blank = Rex's bundled copy)
  rex_app          path to Rex.app for icons (blank = look in /Applications)
  preview_lines    lines of scrollback in the preview (default 70)
  refresh_seconds  cache age that triggers a refresh (default 5)
  icon_aliases     extra program=icon pairs, e.g. "vm-launcher=claude, ipy=python";
                   icon names are Rex's glyphs (claude, neovim, python, terminal, ...)

Each result shows Rex's icon for the program in the tab's focused pane. The icons are
rendered from your installed Rex app on first run, and again after Rex updates.</string>
